    "sessionID": "ses_9997e94bc310453e869b",
    "messageID": "msg_9997e94bc310453e869b_00002",
    "type": "text",
    "text": "turn context: cwd: /work, host: bench-host, date: 2026-10-01\nrouting (preset opus-led): seats you can spawn, with their model and default effort.\n- driver: claude-opus-5-5, medium by default. the session the user talks to.\n- engineer: claude-sonnet-5-5, high by default. writes and changes code in the area it owns and checks its own work.\n- scout: claude-sonnet-5-5, medium by default. reads and searches so you do not have to; reports what it found with exact paths.\n- reviewer: claude-fable-5-1, high by default. reviews and verifies someone else's work on a different model than the author.\n- bulk: claude-sonnet-5-5, low by default. long mechanical reads and rewrites where judgment is cheap.\noff limits: claude-opus-5-5 never runs at xhigh; claude-sonnet-5-5 never runs at max.\na spawn picks a seat, not a model, and may pass an effort within those limits; the seat default applies otherwise.\ndelegation:\n- a child protects your context: reads and log digs you would not want in your own window go to a scout.\n- disjoint pieces of work run in parallel, one writer per area.\n- review and verification are independent when they run on a different seat from the author, ideally a different model; a reviewer can write the check before the engineer starts.\n- long watches (builds, test suites, dev servers) are background jobs with notify, not agents.\n- the decision on the critical path stays with you; read what shapes the plan yourself.\n- work that continues what an existing agent did goes to that agent with message; it keeps its context, a new spawn starts cold.\n- a brief carries the goal, the constraints, the definition of done, the files it owns and the report shape. the stronger the seat, the shorter the brief.\n- when only children or jobs remain, end your turn; their reports wake you.",
    "synthetic": true
   }
  },
  "seq": 1078,
  "epoch": "edf6e3d18c5e"
